{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064051 :question/id #uuid "90010ae5-e211-510f-b188-dc3006926d94" :question/math-academy-id "e-381" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int 5 \\cdot 9^x +3 e^x \\, \\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "Apply the sum rule and take constant factors outside the integrals. Then integrate each exponential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int \\left(5\\cdot 9^x+3e^x\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n&=5\\int 9^x\\,\\mathrm{d}x+3\\int e^x\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\n&=\\frac{5\\cdot 9^x}{\\ln 9}+3e^x+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}
